        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0403" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.75/464: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-11T09:00:00+02:00">April 11, 1939—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Your telegram No. 21, April 7, noon.<anchor n="38a" xml:id="d348-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>It would appear that the occupation of Albania is an eventuality which the
                        Turkish Foreign Office has long contemplated as a possibility <pb
                            facs="0404" n="396" xml:id="pg396"/> but without especial concern, their
                        primary preoccupation being possibility of action on the part of Bulgaria.
                        The event has however brought much closer home to the Turkish public the
                        danger of the present situation.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In view of the conversations held here over the weekend between the
                        Turkish and Rumanian Ministers for Foreign Affairs the results of which are
                        still conjectural, I do not feel in a position to submit more specific
                        comment than was contained in my telegram No. 20, March 27, 7 p.m.,<anchor
                            n="39" xml:id="d348-f2"/> until I shall have been able to consult the
                        Minister for Foreign Affairs as I hope to have the opportunity of doing
                        tomorrow.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
